\n### AvePoint\n\nData/Analytics Founded 2001 · Jersey City, NJ · www.avepoint.com ↗\n\nhigh conf\n\nOverview\n\nAvePoint is a public (NASDAQ: AVPT) data management, security, and governance platform provider focused on the Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace ecosystem. The company is positioning itself as the 'Confidence Platform' for enterprise AI deployment, providing data security, governance, and resilience capabilities critical to organizations deploying AI in production.\n\nProduct\n\nAvePoint Confidence Platform with three core suites: Resilience Suite (data security, ransomware protection), Modernization Suite (legacy data transformation for SaaS), and Control Suite (automated governance). Recent products include AgentPulse Command Center (AI agent governance across M365 and Google Cloud). Serves ~$435M ARR with 9,000+ customers.\n\nTotal Raised\n\n$100M\n\nPublic (NASDAQ: AVPT)\n\nValuation\n\n$2.2B\n\nJun 26, 2019\n\nARR\n\n$435M\n\nAvePoint Q1 2026 ARR $435.2M (public filing).\n\nLast Update\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\nFounded 2001 · Jersey City\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\nAvePoint Q1 2026: 26% revenue growth, targets $1B ARR by 2029\n\nQ1 2026 SaaS revenue $93.4M (+35% YoY), total revenue $117.2M (+26% YoY), ARR $435.2M (+26% YoY). Targets $1B ARR by 2029.\n\nView source ↗\n\nSources\n\nofficial https://www.avepoint.com press https://www.storagenewsletter.com/2026/05/19/avepoint-fiscal-1q26-financial-results/\n\nThe company also acquired Windsurf in 2025.\n\nProduct\n\nDevin: autonomous AI software engineer that plans architecture, writes implementation, runs tests, debugs, and ships pull requests without human hand-holding. Integrates with Slack, GitHub, Linear. SWE-1.6 model is one of the most widely used across the product suite. Pricing dropped from $500/mo to $20/mo + $2.25 per ACU in April 2026. 89% of Cognition's own codebase is now written by Devin.\n\nTotal Raised\n\n$2.5B\n\nSeries D\n\nValuation\n\n$26.0B\n\nMay 27, 2026\n\nARR\n\n$492M\n\nCognition AI Series D announcement, May 2026: $492M ARR.\n\nLast Update\n\nMay 27, 2026\n\nFounded 2023 · San Francisco\n\nLead Investors (latest round)\n\nLux Capital · General Catalyst · 8VC\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nMay 27, 2026\n\nCognition raises $1B at $26B valuation; 89% of own code written by Devin\n\nSeries D led by Lux Capital, General Catalyst, 8VC. Run-rate revenue $492M, enterprise usage grew 50% MoM for 6 months. 89% of Cognition's own code committed by Devin.\n\nView source ↗\nQ1 2026 revenue crossed $1B for the first time ($1.006B, +32% YoY), with total ARR exceeding $4B. AI integrations now used by 6,500+ customers (20% of total) representing 80% of ARR. Five of 26 products are over $100M ARR each.\n\nProduct\n\nUnified observability and security across infrastructure, applications, data, models. Key products: Bits AI (SRE Agent, Security Analyst, Dev Agent — autonomously analyzing alerts and generating fixes), GPU Monitoring, MCP Server (real-time access for AI agents), Experiments (A/B testing), Cloud SIEM. 4,550 customers with $100K+ ARR. Strategic partnerships with Sakana AI (Japan) and others.\n\nTotal Raised\n\n$147M\n\nIPO (2019)\n\nValuation\n\n—\n\nSep 19, 2019\n\nARR\n\n$4.0B\n\nDatadog Q1 2026 earnings: total ARR >$4B.\n\nLast Update\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\nFounded 2010 · New York\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\nDatadog Q1 2026: First $1B revenue quarter, $4B+ ARR\n\nRevenue $1.006B (+32% YoY), ARR exceeds $4B. 6,500+ customers use AI integrations (80% of ARR). 4,550 customers with $100K+ ARR. Launched MCP Server, Bits AI Security Agent, GPU Monitoring. Partnership with Sakana AI for Japan.\n\nView source ↗\n\nSources\n\nofficial https://www.datadoghq.com official https://investors.datadoghq.com\n\n### Decart\n\nVideo/Image AI Founded 2023 · Tel Aviv, Israel · www.decart.ai ↗\n\nhigh conf\n\nOverview\n\nDecart is an Israeli AI research lab specializing in real-time video and world models. The company raised $300M at a $4B valuation led by Radical Ventures, with strategic backing from NVIDIA, Adobe Ventures, Toyota Ventures, and OpenAI co-founder Andrej Karpathy. Decart's core innovation is a real-time inference stack (DOS) that makes world models production-viable.\n\nProduct\n\nThree products built on DOS infrastructure: (1) DOS 2.0 — optimization platform for AI workloads, processing 1,600+ tokens/sec (8x industry average) for agents and 100 FPS for video. (2) Lucy — real-time world model for video modification (sub-30ms response for smart mirrors, virtual try-on, gaming). (3) Oasis — 3D environment generator for robotics training and simulation. Customers include Amazon, eBay, Twitch creators.\n\nTotal Raised\n\n$450M\n\nStrategic\n\nValuation\n\n$4.0B\n\nMay 18, 2026\n\nARR\n\n—\n\nGenerating 'significant revenue' from DOS licensing; specific ARR undisclosed.\n\nLast Update\n\nMay 18, 2026\n\nFounded 2023 · Tel Aviv\n\nLead Investors (latest round)\n\nRadical Ventures\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nMay 18, 2026\n\nDecart raises $300M at $4B valuation; launches DOS 2.0\n\nNew round at nearly $4B. DOS 2.0 enables 1,600+ tokens/sec inference and 100 FPS video. Strategic customers include Amazon.\n\nView source ↗\n\nSources\n\nofficial https://www.decart.ai press https://siliconangle.com/2026/05/18/decart-raises-300m-ai-optimization-software-world-models/\n\n\nLast Update\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\nFounded 2019 · Palo Alto\n\nLead Investors (latest round)\n\nHumain (Saudi PIF)\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\nLuma AI: CEO sees first AI-assisted film coming in 2026\n\nLuma AI secures funding from Saudi-backed Humain. CEO Amit Jain predicts first 'significantly aided by AI' film will arrive in 2026. Ray 3 used by 5 of 6 major studios.\n\nView source ↗\n\nSources\n\nofficial https://lumalabs.ai press https://www.cnbc.com/2026/05/19/luma-ai-cnbc-disruptor-50-ranking.html\n\n### Manus AI\n\nAI Agents Founded 2022 · Singapore · manus.im ↗\n\nhigh conf\n\nOverview\n\nManus is an autonomous AI agent platform that independently executes complex multi-step tasks based on natural language instructions. Originally incubated by Beijing Butterfly Effect Technology, it relocated core team to Singapore in July 2025 and reached $100M+ ARR by December 2025. Meta acquired Manus in December 2025 for $2-3B, but the deal was blocked by China's NDRC in April 2026, leading to a buyback effort at the same $2B valuation.\nJust released Kimi K3, the world's largest open-weight model (2.8T parameters).\n\nProduct\n\nKimi K3 (flagship, 2.8T params, open-weight, comparable to US frontier models). Kimi K2.7 Code (specialized coding, $0.95/$4 per million tokens). Kimi K2.6 (general-purpose, second-most used on OpenRouter). Chat interface at kimi.com. Backed by Alibaba, Tencent, Meituan. Plans Hong Kong IPO.\n\nTotal Raised\n\n$3.9B\n\nSeries in talks (June 2026)\n\nValuation\n\n$20.0B\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\nARR\n\n—\n\nMoonshot does not publicly disclose ARR.\n\nLast Update\n\nJul 17, 2026\n\nFounded 2023 · Beijing\n\nLead Investors (latest round)\n\nMeituan (reported)\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nJul 17, 2026\n\nMoonshot launches Kimi K3, world's largest open-weight AI model (2.8T params)\n\nKimi K3 has 2.8T parameters, 75% larger than DeepSeek V4 Pro. Performance approaches US frontier Fable model. Full open weights scheduled for July 27. Priced at $3/$15 per million tokens.\n\nView source ↗\n\nSources\n\nofficial https://www.moonshot.ai press https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/07/chinas-moonshot-ai-raises-2b-at-20b-valuation-as-demand-for-open-source-ai-skyrockets/\n\nValuation\n\n$7.5B\n\nOct 1, 2025\n\nARR\n\n—\n\nPre-revenue research stage.\n\nLast Update\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\nFounded 2025 · San Francisco\n\nLead Investors (latest round)\n\nAndreessen Horowitz\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\nPeriodic Labs in talks for $500M+ at $7.5B valuation\n\nForbes reports Periodic Labs raising at $7.5B, 6x increase from seed in 8 months. Led by AMP (Anney Midha). Building AI scientists + autonomous robotic labs.\n\nView source ↗\n\nSources\n\nofficial https://periodic.com press https://siliconangle.com/2025/10/01/periodic-labs-raises-300m-accelerate-scientific-research-ai/\n\n### Preferred Networks\n\nAI Infrastructure Founded 2014 · Tokyo, Japan · www.preferred.jp ↗\n\nhigh conf\n\nOverview\n\nPreferred Networks (PFN) is Japan's leading independent AI company, established in 2014 by University of Tokyo computer scientists. A vertically integrated developer of AI semiconductors, computing infrastructure, generative AI, and specific AI solutions. \nTotal Raised\n\n$2.0B\n\nSeed\n\nValuation\n\n$12.0B\n\nJul 1, 2025\n\nARR\n\n—\n\nPre-revenue research stage.\n\nLast Update\n\nMay 26, 2026\n\nFounded 2025 · San Francisco\n\nLead Investors (latest round)\n\nAndreessen Horowitz\n\nDevelopment Timeline\n\nMay 26, 2026\n\nThinking Machines launches 'interaction models' category with TML-Interaction-Small\n\nNew model category: AI that processes input and generates output simultaneously. 0.40s response time matching human conversation. Infrastructure deals with Nvidia and Google.\n\nView source ↗\n\nSources\n\nofficial https://thinkingmachines.ai press https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/22/exclusive-google-deepens-thinking-machines-lab-ties-with-new-multi-billion-dollar-deal/\n\n### Wonderful AI\n\nAI Agents Founded 2025 · Tel Aviv, Israel · www.wonderful.ai ↗\n\nhigh conf\n\nOverview\n\nWonderful is an Israeli enterprise AI agent platform founded in 2025 by Bar Winkler (CEO) and Roey Lalazar (CTO). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUniformly Positive Scalar Curvature on Manifold Interiors (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.07608)\nciteturn39235academia4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Date: Tue Oct  6 01:51:07 2026 ... Further, let $X$ be a compact oriented smooth manifold of dimension $5$, $6$, or $7$. ... In dimensions $6$ and $7$, the metric may moreover be chosen to be a product near the boundary.\nTitle: Uniformly Positive Scalar Curvature on Manifold Interiors\nAuthors: Shuli Chen\nDate: Tue Oct  6 01:51:07 2026\n\nWe obtain topological obstructions to the existence of a complete Riemannian metric with uniformly positive scalar curvature on the interiors of certain 4-manifolds using Seiberg--Witten theory. In particular, no punctured blowups of a homotopy K3 manifold admit complete metrics of uniformly positive scalar curvature. Further, let $X$ be a compact oriented smooth manifold of dimension $5$, $6$, or $7$. We show that if $\\operatorname{Int}X$ admits a complete metric of uniformly positive scalar curvature, then $X$ admits a positive scalar curvature metric with minimal boundary. In dimensions $6$ and $7$, the metric may moreover be chosen to be a product near the boundary. In dimension 5, under additional hypotheses and after possibly changing the smooth structure on $X$, one can likewise obtain a positive scalar curvature metric that is a product near the boundary."
